$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }t\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-6})+(\goldD{7})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{\dfrac{1}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $g\left(\blueD{\dfrac{1}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
g\left(\blueD{\dfrac{1}{2}}\right)&=\left(\blueD{\dfrac{1}{2}}\right)^2-\left(\blueD{\dfrac{1}{2}}\right)-42
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{4}-\dfrac{1}{2}-42
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{169}{4}
\end{align}$
